# viz: integrals shaded, Riemann sums, accumulation, solids of revolution;
# nofile prints the report and a checksum instead of NAME.gif
# area: exact from the antiderivative, numeric always, signed parts
area x^2 from 0 to 4 nofile
area sin x from 0 to 2pi nofile
area x^2 - 1 nofile
area x^2 and x nofile
area sin x and cos x from 0 to 2pi nofile
area log(x) from 0 to 1 nofile
area 1/x from 0 to 1 nofile
area 1/x from -1 to 1 nofile
# Riemann sums: one n, or n = 1, 2, 4 ... 64 animated
area x^2 from 0 to 4 riemann 8 left nofile
area x^2 from 0 to 4 riemann nofile
area sin x from 0 to 2pi riemann 12 trapezoid nofile
area x^3 - 3x from -2 to 2 riemann 5 simpson nofile
# the accumulation function
area x^2 from 0 to 2 accumulate frames 12 nofile
# solids of revolution: washers, shells, other axes
revolve x^2 from 0 to 2 about x frames 8 nofile
revolve sqrt(x) from 0 to 4 about x still nofile
revolve x^2 from 0 to 2 about y still nofile
revolve x and x^2 from 0 to 1 about x-axis still nofile
revolve sin x about x still nofile
revolve x^2 from 0 to 1 about y = -1 still nofile
revolve x^2 from 0 to 1 about x = 2 still nofile
revolve sin x and 0 from 0 to pi about y = -1 still nofile
revolve x^2 about y still nofile
revolve sqrt(x) from 0 to 4 about x rotate frames 6 nofile
# text only: volume, surface area, arc length, centroid
volume x^2 from 0 to 1
volume x^2 from 0 to 2 about x shell
volume x from -1 to 2 about y
surfacearea x from 0 to 1
arclength x^2 from 0 to 1
arclength sqrt(1 - x^2) from 0 to 1
centroid x^2 and x
g(x) = x^3
centroid g from 0 to 1
# English
slice of integral f(x) = x^2 at 0 till 4 nofile
area under x^2 from 0 to 4 nofile
shade the integral of sin x from 0 to pi nofile
show the area between x^2 and x from 0 to 1 nofile
a left riemann sum of x^2 from 0 to 4 with 8 rectangles nofile
the midpoint rule for sin x from 0 to pi nofile
the accumulation function of cos x from 0 to 2pi frames 6 nofile
revolve f(x) = x^2 in x-axis still nofile
rotate x^2 around the y axis still nofile
solid of revolution of sqrt x from 0 to 4 still nofile
spin sin x about the x-axis still nofile
revolve x and x^2 from 0 to 1 about the x-axis using washers still nofile
rotate the region between x and x^2 about the line y = 2 still nofile
volume of revolution of x^2 from 0 to 1 about the y-axis
the surface area of revolution of x from 0 to 1
arc length of x^2 from 0 to 1
the centroid of the region between x^2 and x
# errors
area
area x*y from 0 to 1
revolve x^2 about z
area x^2 from 0 to 4 about x
revolve x^2 riemann 4
